@* The task list screen: every report's tasks, by due date, with the status
   filter and the one action a task takes.

   ../nedss/docs/functional/session-012-investigation-admin-contacts-notes.md
   records the legacy Tasks section on a report's Notes tab, with a "Show all
   tasks" filter beside it: the filter is there because a worker's tasks are
   not read a report at a time. This screen is that reading — the same panel
   the Notes tab shows, asked for every report rather than for one.

   Adding a task is not here. A task is recorded against a report, and this
   screen has none in hand: it is opened from the app bar rather than from a
   case. The panel offers the "+ Add Task" form on the Notes tab, where the
   report is known. *@
@page "/tasks"

<PageTitle>Tasks — Survsys</PageTitle>

<MudText id="tasks-heading" HtmlTag="h1" Typo="Typo.h4" GutterBottom="true">
    Tasks
</MudText>

<MudText id="tasks-lead-in" Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mb-4">
    The tasks raised against every case, soonest due first. Show the ones still
    to do, the ones done, or all of them, and complete a task once it is done.
    A task is added from the Notes tab of the case it is about.
</MudText>

<TasksPanel />
